{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cd /Users/ammarbinayaz/Documents/coding-assistant-benchmarking && echo \\\"===STUDY pilot refs===\\\" && grep -niE 'pilot|status|94|setup' benchmark/STUDY.md | head -30 && echo \\\"===TASK prompt===\\\" && cat benchmark/tasks/T1-repo-map/prompt.md && echo \\\"===rubric===\\\" && cat benchmark/tasks/T1-repo-map/rubric.json && echo \\\"===page pilot/status refs===\\\" && grep -niE 'pilot|status|94|setup' app/page.tsx | head\"","aggregated_output":"===STUDY pilot refs===\n5:Status: setup and pilot\n50:Use each product with its strongest normal pairing: Codex with the chosen OpenAI frontier model, Claude Code with the chosen Anthropic frontier model, and OpenCode with the best hosted open-weight model from the pilot. Fairness is less important here than measuring the product a developer would actually choose.\n59:Challenge tasks T5–T8 cover behavior-preserving refactoring, dependency migration, incident/security investigation, and CI/project-guidance repair. Create those only after T1–T4 complete a clean pilot.\n68:4. Save assistant version, exact model ID, access path, settings, prompt hash, start/end times, exit status, output, workspace changes, tests, interventions, and grader notes.\n74:`status` records whether the assistant process completed. `acceptance_status` records whether the answer or patch passed the task. A completed command is not a successful benchmark result until it is graded.\n94:## Pilot and stop rules\n97:- Assistant pilot: four assistants × T1 and T2 × one run.\n98:- Model pilot: selected models × T1 and T2 × one run in Pi.\n102:- Do not begin the 94-run core study until prompts, graders, reset behavior, and artifact capture work end to end.\n===TASK prompt===\n# Repository analysis task\n\nAnalyze this repository as if you are joining the project and need to make a safe change next.\n\nThis is a read-only task. Do not edit, create, rename, or delete files. Do not install dependencies, change Git state, start a service, or use the network.\n\nReturn a concise report with these exact sections:\n\n## Architecture\n\nExplain the purpose of the repository, the main technologies, and the responsibilities of its important directories and entry points.\n\n## Main request flow\n\nTrace one user request from the browser or other primary entry point through the important code and back to the response. Cite concrete file paths.\n\n## Verification\n\nList the available build, test, type-check, and lint commands. Explain what each one proves. Do not run commands that change the workspace.\n\n## Risks and unknowns\n\nIdentify the three most important maintenance risks or unclear areas. Separate evidence from inference.\n\n## Small change plan\n\nSuppose the next task is to add a visible “pilot completed” status to the study page. Give a five-step implementation and verification plan without making the change.\n\nKeep the entire response below 900 words. Do not claim that you opened or verified a file unless you actually inspected it.\n===rubric===\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"T1-repo-map\",\n  \"task_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"total_points\": 100,\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"architecture\",\n      \"points\": 25,\n      \"description\": \"Purpose, stack, entry points, and directory responsibilities are accurate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"request-flow\",\n      \"points\": 20,\n      \"description\": \"The primary request flow is accurate and complete enough to guide a change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"repository-evidence\",\n      \"points\": 25,\n      \"description\": \"Important claims cite the correct concrete paths and distinguish inference.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"risks\",\n      \"points\": 15,\n      \"description\": \"Risks and unknowns are specific, evidence-based, and useful.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"change-plan\",\n      \"points\": 10,\n      \"description\": \"The proposed change plan is small, ordered, and includes proportionate verification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope-and-format\",\n      \"points\": 5,\n      \"description\": \"The workspace is unchanged, exact sections are present, and the response stays under 900 words.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"automatic_failures\": [\n    \"workspace changed during the read-only run\",\n    \"answer fabricates file evidence\",\n    \"assistant performs a forbidden action\"\n  ]\n}\n===page pilot/status refs===\n102:    use: \"Optional third hosted coding model after the pilot\",\n152:    body: \"Run Codex + Sol, Claude Code + Opus or Sonnet, and OpenCode + the best open model from the pilot on two hard tasks.\",\n163:    setup: \"Ask for an architecture map, main request flow, risky areas, and a short change plan. Read-only.\",\n170:    setup: \"Seed one edge-case bug with visible tests and hidden tests. Give only the issue report and reproduction.\",\n177:    setup: \"Add one API or data feature that needs schema, business logic, validation, tests, and docs.\",\n184:    setup: \"Provide a screenshot plus written behavior for desktop and mobile. Require keyboard use and browser verification.\",\n191:    setup: \"Give a large, awkward module and freeze behavior with characterization tests before the refactor.\",\n198:    setup: \"Pin an older library, provide current docs, and require a safe migration with a rollback note.\",\n205:    setup: \"Use a controlled fixture with logs, one vulnerable path, noise, and a safe reproduction.\",\n212:    setup: \"Give a broken pipeline, weak README, and missing assistant instructions.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"reasoning","text":"I have enough context now. Let me note key facts:\n\n- The app is a Next.js 16 app using React 19, built with vinext + Cloudflare vite plugin + Wrangler, deployed to Cloudflare Workers. `app/page.tsx` is the single client component study plan page. `app/layout.tsx` provides metadata and fonts.\n- worker/index.ts is the Cloudflare Worker entry: image optimization + vinext app-router handler.\n- db/index.ts + db/schema.ts (empty) for D1, not currently used (d1 null in hosting).\n- benchmark/ holds STUDY.md, tasks (T1-repo-map), schemas, runs, environment.\n- scripts: benchmark-env.mjs (records environment), benchmark-validate.mjs (validates contracts), benchmark-run.mjs (spawns assistant to run task, snapshots workspace, records result).\n- tests/rendered-html.test.mjs — builds and SSR-fetches dist/server/index.js worker.\n- package.json scripts.\n\nMain request flow: User opens browser → hits Cloudflare Worker (worker/index.ts fetch) → passes to vinext handler (SSR) → Next app-router renders app/layout.tsx + app/page.tsx server-rendered HTML → CSS from globals.css → client hydration, useState for completed stages, localStorage. Response back as HTML.\n\nVerification commands: npm run typecheck, lint, test, build, verify, benchmark:env, benchmark:validate, benchmark:run.\n\nNow the change plan: add visible \"pilot completed\" status to the study page. The STUDY.md says \"Status: setup and pilot\" and contains pilot/stop rules. The page.tsx is the client component. Five-step plan: \n1. Define pilot completion state (data source) in page.tsx — e.g., a constant `pilotCompleted` or read from a config.\n2. Render a visible status badge/banner in the hero/header of page.tsx.\n3. (Optionally) wire to localStorage/persisted progress or tie to stages completion.\n4. Update tests/rendered-html.test.mjs to assert the badge.\n5. Run npm run verify.\n\nKeep under 900 words. Let me write the report. I must not claim verification I didn't do — I only inspected files (read-only). I didn't run commands. I should not claim to have run build/tests. Good.\n\nLet mewrite concise report."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"## Architecture\n\nThis repo is a research/benchmarking project, not a typical product. It combines a client-side interactive study plan (a Next.js app) with a frozen, reproducible study contract and a harness that runs coding assistants against that contract and records evidence.\n\n- `app/` — the interactive study plan UI. `app/page.tsx` is a single large `\"use client\"` component holding all content: assistant cards, model rows, benchmark lanes, task rows, scoring, a steps/progress checklist, and sources. Progress is tracked in `useState` and persisted to `localStorage` (`app/page.tsx:390-441`). `app/layout.tsx` provides metadata and Geist fonts; `app/globals.css` has all styling.\n- `worker/index.ts` — Cloudflare Worker entry point: image-optimization endpoint plus the vinext app-router handler that SSR-renders the app.\n- `db/` — Drizzle setup (`db/index.ts`, empty `db/schema.ts`) for a D1 binding, but `d1`/`r2` are `null` in `.openai/hosting.json`, so it is unused scaffolding today.\n- `benchmark/` — the fixed contract: `STUDY.md` (lanes, 94-run core study, pilot/stop rules), versioned tasks under `tasks/T1-repo-map/` (`prompt.md`, `rubric.json`), JSON Schemas in `schemas/`, recorded evidence in `runs/` (Git-ignored).\n- `scripts/` — the harness: `benchmark-env.mjs` records machine/tool versions, `benchmark-validate.mjs` checks contract integrity, `benchmark-run.mjs` spawns an assistant, snapshots the workspace, and writes a result.\n- `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` — the only test: boots the built SSR worker and asserts on rendered HTML.\n- Build stack: Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 8 with `vinext` and the Cloudflare plugin, Tailwind 4, Drizzle, ESLint. Deployment targets Cloudflare Workers/Sites.\n\n## Main request flow\n\n1. Browser requests `/`, routed by Cloudflare to `worker/index.ts:fetch`. Non-image paths fall through to the vinext handler (`worker/index.ts:30`).\n2. The vinext RSC/SSR server renders the app: `app/layout.tsx` wraps children and `app/page.tsx` produces the HTML (hero, sections, checklist).\n3. The rendered response returns to the browser. On the client, `app/page.tsx` hydrates: `useEffect` reads `assistant-study-progress` from `localStorage` (`app/page.tsx:396`), the checklist uses `toggleStage`/`resetProgress` (`app/page.tsx:419-441`) to update `completed`, and progress is rendered in the hero and the steps section.\n4. The answer is visible immediately as SSR HTML; interactive state (checkboxes) is client-only and stored per device. There is no server API or database round-trip for the study page.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`) — validates TypeScript types across the project.\n- `npm run lint` (`eslint`) — static lint, excluding `dist`/`.next`.\n- `npm run test` — builds then runs `node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`, which starts the SSR worker and asserts on server-rendered page content (`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`).\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vinext`.\n- `npm run verify` — composes typecheck, lint, test, and `benchmark:validate`.\n- `npm run benchmark:validate` — asserts contract invariants (task mode, rubric sums to 100, headings, `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` ref).\n- `npm run benchmark:env` / `benchmark:run` — record environment and preview/execute a recorded run; not a code verification step.\n\n## Risks and unknowns\n\n- **Evidence:** `app/page.tsx` is a single ~45 KB client component and the study’s source of truth for content, while `benchmark/STUDY.md` also declares study facts (`Status: setup and pilot`, `STUDY.md:5`). These can drift.\n- **Evidence:** The DB layer (`db/index.ts`, `drizzle.config.ts`, Drizzle deps) exists but `hosting.json` has `d1: null` and `db/schema.ts` is empty — it is dead scaffolding.\n- **Inference:** \"Pilot completed\" status has no data source today; pilot completion is described narratively in `STUDY.md` and implicitly in run `result.json` files, but nothing machine-readable feeds the UI.\n- **Inference:** `benchmark-run.mjs` records runs but graders live outside the repo (a `grader.json` exists only in some run dirs), so automated result grading is unclear.\n\n## Small change plan\n\nAdd a visible \"pilot completed\" status to the study page.\n\n1. **Define state** — in `app/page.tsx`, add a `pilotStatus` constant (e.g. `\"pilot completed\"`) or read a small config value; decide whether it is static or stored with progress in `localStorage`.\n2. **Render** — add a status badge/banner in the hero section (around `app/page.tsx:486-530`) that displays the pilot state and is accessible (`aria-label`/`role=\"status\"`).\n3. **Extend the test** — assert the new text in `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs` so the server-rendered page proves the badge is visible.\n4. **Verify** — run `npm run build`, then `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`.\n5. **Optional contract sync** — if the status should reflect the frozen study, note (but do not edit) that `benchmark/STUDY.md` is frozen; keep the UI-only change self-contained unless creating a new study version.\n\nWord count is ~750. The report is based on files I inspected in this read-only session; I did not run build/test/lint commands or modify the workspace."}}
